          %p
            The
            %em ring of adeles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+field"} global field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            – in particular of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            – is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restricted+product"} restricted product
            of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completions"} formal completions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_v
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            at all its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/places"} places
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
            of components have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
            greater than 1. (This has a useful geometric interpretation and motivation by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy"} function field analogy
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#FunctionFieldAnalogy"} below
          %p
            In particular the ring of adeles of the rational numbers is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+integers"} p-adic integers
            (including the “prime at infinity”).
          %p
            In classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+number+theory"} algebraic number theory
            one embeds a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+field"} number field
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion+of+a+ring"} completions
            at its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/archimedean+absolute+values"} archimedean absolute values
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proofs"} proofs
            of several fundamental
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theorems"} theorems
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+integers"} algebraic integers
            in the number field embed discretely and co-compactly into this
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+in+a+vector+space"} lattice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
            (modulo
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+analysis"} Fourier analysis
            where Poisson summation applied to the lattice has classical implications for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+functions"} theta functions
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+functions"} zeta functions
          %p
            It was noticed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claude+Chevalley"} Claude Chevalley
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Weil"} André Weil
            that the situation is made even better if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+field"} number field
            itself is embedded in the cartesian product of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completions"} formal completions
            at all of its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+values"} absolute values
            = succeed "," do
              %em adeles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} units
            of this ring are called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideles"} ideles
          %p
            When considering the adeles and ideles, it is their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            as much as their algebraic structure that is of interest. Many important results in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
            translate into simple statements about the topologies of the adeles and ideles. For example, the finiteness of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal+class+group"} ideal class group
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirichlet+unit+theorem"} Dirichlet unit theorem
            are equivalent to a certain quotient of the ideles being compact and discrete.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Weston"}> Weston, p. 1
            )
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The concept of a
            %em ring of adeles
            (older synonym: ring of valuation vectors) makes sense for any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+field"} global field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+extension"} field extension
            of either the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            or of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field"} function field
            over a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+field"} finite field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            themselves is the classical case which we discuss first in
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ForTheRationalNumbers"} For the rational numbers
          %p Then we consider the definition more generally
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ForAnyNumberField"} For a number field
          %p and finally in full generality
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => ""}> For a global field
              \.
          %h3#ForTheRationalNumbers For the rational numbers
          %p
            We start off very simply with the algebraic description of the adele ring over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
          #RingOfAdeles.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The ring of
              %em integral adeles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Z}}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+completion+of+the+integers"} profinite completion of the integers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{\mathbb{Z}}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ×
                    %mover
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Z}}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\mathbb{R} \times \widehat{\mathbb{Z}}
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %em ring of adeles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}
              (or just
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔸
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
              of the ring of integral adeles, hence its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℚ
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi ℚ
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℤ
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\mathbb{Q}
                    \\otimes_\mathbb{Z}
                    \\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
          %p This definition has various equivalent reformulations which are often useful.
          #ProfiniteIntegersAsProductOverpAdics.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              By
              %a{:href => "profinite+completion+of+the+integers#AsProductOverAlsoPAdicIntegers"} this proposition
              we have that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+completion+of+the+integers"} profinite completion of the integers
              is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+integers"} p-adic integers
              as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              ranges over all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+numbers"} prime numbers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi prime
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat \mathbb{Z} \simeq \underset{p\;prime}{\prod} \mathbb{Z}_p
            %p
              Using this in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RingOfAdeles"}
              says that the ring of integral adeles is the product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ×
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi prime
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Z}}
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbb{R} \times
                    \\underset{p\;prime}{\prod} \mathbb{Z}_p
                    \\,.
          %p From this one obtains the following equivalent characterization:
          #RationalRingOfAdelesAsRestrictedProduct.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The ring of adeles
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔸
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RingOfAdeles"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restricted+product"} restricted product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod^\prime
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+rational+numbers"} p-adic rational numbers
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mi p
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_p \to \mathbb{Q}_p
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℚ
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ×
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                            %mo ′
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi prime
                    %msub
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}
                    \=
                    \\mathbb{R} \times \underset{p \; prime}{\prod^\prime} \mathbb{Q}_p
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProfiniteIntegersAsProductOverpAdics"}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              to be computed is equivalently
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℚ
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℚ
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ×
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi prime
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mi p
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbb{Q}\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}}
                    \\left(
                    \\mathbb{R} \times
                    \\underset{p \; prime}{\prod} \mathbb{Z}_p
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now notice that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} unit
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_p
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is not a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+factor"} prime factor
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_p) \in \underset{p}{\prod} \mathbb{Z}_p
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mi c
                        %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{c}{d} \in \mathbb{Q}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+factors"} prime factors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              the tensor product element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mi c
                      %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℤ
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{c}{d} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} a_p \in \mathbb{Q}_p
              contains a non-vanishing negative power of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              and is hence not in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              that do not appear as prime factors in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              it is.
          %p Finally notice:
          #AsProductOverPlaces.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+numbers"} prime numbers
              correspond to the non-archimedean
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/places"} places
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/place+at+infinity"} place at infinity
              = succeed "\u201D," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion+of+a+ring"} completion
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
              at which is the real numbers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} = \mathbb{Q}_\infty
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RationalRingOfAdelesAsRestrictedProduct"}
              is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restricted+product"} restricted product
              over all real places of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completion"} formal completion
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
              at this place
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℚ
                    %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                            %mo ′
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Places
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}
                    \\simeq
                    \\underset{p \in Places(\mathbb{Z})}{\prod^{\prime}} \mathbb{Q}_p
                    \\,.
            %p
              Considering this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restricted+product"} restricted product
              not just in bare
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
              but in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+rings"} topological rings
              yields the right structure of a topological ring on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} locally compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
              commutative ring. In particular, it is complete with respect to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniform space
              structure.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The restricted product is a filtered colimit of a system of
              %em open
              inclusions between locally compact Hausdorff rings, and is therefore itself locally compact Hausdorff. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_\alpha
              is a Cauchy net, then for all sufficiently large
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha, \beta
              the differences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi α
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_\alpha - x_\beta
              lie in a compact neighborhood of the identity. Holding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              fixed, the limit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi α
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_\alpha x_\alpha - x_\beta
              exists by compactness; if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is this limit, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x + x_\beta
              is the limit of the Cauchy net.
          %p
            If one omits the factor of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} = \mathbb{Q}_\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %em ring of finite adeles
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mi f
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                          %mo ′
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi prime
                  %msub
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^f \coloneqq \underset{p \; prime}{\prod^\prime} \mathbb{Q}_p
                  \\,.
          %p
            All of this generalizes to any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+field"} number field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %h3#ForAnyNumberField For a number field
          %p Let
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                be a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+field"} number field
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O} = \mathcal{O}_k
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+integers"} ring of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+integers"} algebraic integers
                in
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                be its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/places"} places
                (equivalence classes of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+values"} absolute values
                on
                = succeed ");" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒪
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\subset P
                be the set of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/archimedean+valuation"} archimedean
                places;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_v
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completion"} formal completion
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                at
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\in P
          %p Notice that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in S
                then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_v
                is isomorphic to one of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+fields"} local fields
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
                or
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℂ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            %li
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \notin S
                then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_v
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field"} local field
                with an open compact subring
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_v
                consisting of elements of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                or less.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+field"} number field
              %em integral adeles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_{\mathcal{O}}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+completion"} profinite completion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{\mathcal{O}}
              with all the archimedean completions,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi 𝒪
                    %mo ≔
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ×
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi v
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{A}_\mathcal{O}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\widehat{\mathcal{O}} \times \prod_{v \in S} k_v
                    \\,,
            %p
              and the
              %em ring of adeles
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mi k
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi k
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi 𝒪
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mi 𝒪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k \coloneqq k \otimes_\mathcal{O} \mathbb{A}_\mathcal{O}
          %p It may be shown that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo ^
                  %mo ≅
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{\mathcal{O}} \cong \prod_{v \notin S} \mathcal{O}_v
          %p
            where each non-archimedean place
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            may be identified with a prime ideal
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            as the localization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            obtained by inverting all nonzero elements
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathcal{O}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            may be written as a filtered colimit of a system of inclusions of localizations:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo ≅
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mi x
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \cong colim_x \; \mathcal{O}[x^{-1}].
          %p Componentwise, we may calculate
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi 𝒪
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mtext if
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi p
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mtext if
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∉
                          %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathcal{O}[x^{-1}] \otimes_\mathcal{O} \mathcal{O}_p &amp; = &amp; k_p &amp; \text{if}\; x \in p \\
                  \&amp; = &amp; \mathcal{O}_p &amp; \text{if}\; x \notin p
                  }
          %p and so
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi 𝒪
                          %mover
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo ^
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi 𝒪
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi P
                              %mo \
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi S
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mi p
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi p
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∉
                              %mi p
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathcal{O}[x^{-1}] \otimes_\mathcal{O} \widehat{\mathcal{O}} &amp; \cong &amp; \mathcal{O}[x^{-1}] \otimes_\mathcal{O} \prod_{p \in P \backslash\; S} \mathcal{O}_p \\
                  \&amp; \cong &amp; (\prod_{x \in p} k_p) \times (\prod_{x \notin p} \mathcal{O}_p)
                  }
          %p Putting these facts together,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %mover
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo ^
                  %mo ≅
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mi x
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi p
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi p
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \otimes_\mathcal{O} \widehat{\mathcal{O}} \cong colim_x\; (\prod_{x \in p} k_p) \times (\prod_{x \notin p} \mathcal{O}_p)
          %p whence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "left left left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi k
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi 𝒪
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔸
                          %mi 𝒪
                      %mtd
                        %mo ≅
                      %mtd
                        %mi k
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi 𝒪
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mrow
                              %mi v
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi S
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi v
                          %mo ×
                          %mover
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo ^
                          %mo )
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                      %mtd
                        %mo ≅
                      %mtd
                        %msub
                          %mi colim
                          %mi x
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
                            %mi v
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi S
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi v
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo :
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi p
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo :
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∉
                            %mi p
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{lll}
                  k \otimes_\mathcal{O} \mathbb{A}_\mathcal{O} &amp; \cong &amp; k \otimes_\mathcal{O} \left(\prod_{v \in S} k_v \times \widehat{\mathcal{O}}\right) \\
                  \&amp; \cong &amp; colim_x \; \prod_{v \in S} k_v \times (\prod_{p: x \in p} k_p) \times (\prod_{p: x \notin p} \mathcal{O}_p)
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            where each component of the filtered diagram is locally compact (a product of finitely many locally compact and infinitely many compact spaces) in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topology"} product topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            over the resulting diagram of open inclusions, the result is again a locally compact ring. In this way the ring of adeles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k
            is topologized.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              The topology on the adele ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k
              is strictly finer than the subspace topology inherited from its natural inclusion into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{v \in P} k_v
              with the product topology. For example,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mo \
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\prod_{v \in S} k_v) \times \prod_{p \in P \backslash\; S} \mathcal{O}_p
              is open in the ring of adeles, but not in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi P
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{v \in P} k_v
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
              of the ring of adeles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k
              is called the group of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideles"} ideles
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝕀
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}_k
          %p
            Under the subspace topology inherited from
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝕀
                    %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝕀
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{-1}: \mathbb{I}_k \to \mathbb{I}_k
            to be continuous (and in fact it isn’t!), so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝕀
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}_k
            isn’t a topological group when topologized this way. However, we can endow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝕀
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}_k
            with the subspace topology given by the embedding
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕀
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}_k \to \mathbb{A}_k \times \mathbb{A}_k: x \mapsto (x, x^{-1})
            %em This is the topology on the ideles.
          %p
            Alternatively, for each finite
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \subset P
            containing the set of archimedean places
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝕀
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mi T
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi T
                  %msubsup
                    %mi k
                    %mi v
                    %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi T
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi v
                    %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}_{k, T} = (\prod_{v \in T} k_v^\times) \times (\prod_{v \notin T} \mathcal{O}_v^\times)
          %p
            (noting that each unit group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi v
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_v^\times
            is compact), and the idele group can be described as the colimit over a filtered system of open inclusions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝕀
                    %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mi T
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝕀
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}_k = colim_T \; \mathbb{I}_{k, T}
          %p and indeed the idele topology coincides with the filtered colimit topology.
          %h3#ForAGlobalField For a global field
          %p
            Fully generally, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+field"} global field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            for its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/places"} places
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_v
            for its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completion"} formal completion
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in P
          #AsRestrictedProduct.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em ring of adeles
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+field"} global field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restricted+product"} restricted product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{A}_k \coloneqq \underset{v \in P}{\prod} k_v
            %p
              where the restriction is to elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi v
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_v)_{v\in P}
              of the actual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              whose components have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
              at most unity –
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert x_v\vert} \leq 1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            %p
              This is topologized in the same way as discussed
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#ForAnyNumberField"} above
          %p
            Reviews includes (
            %a{:href => "#Mathew10"}> Mathew 10
            ).
          %p
            In the function field case, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is a finite extension of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p(T)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(k)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+closure"} integral closure
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            of the subring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p[T] \hookrightarrow \mathbb{F}_p(T)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_{\mathcal{O}(k)}
            may be defined to be the product of all the completions of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(k)
            over all the places of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k = k \otimes_{\mathcal{O}(k)} \mathbb{A}_{\mathcal{O}(k)}
          %p where the right side is again interpreted as a colimit in the category of topological rings of a diagram consisting of compact topological rings and open inclusions between them.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#basic_results Basic results
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Under the natural inclusion
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi k
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: k \to \mathbb{A}_k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is discrete, and the quotient topology on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k/k
              is compact.
          %p
            As an additive topological group, there is a natural pairing on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi k
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -, - \rangle: \mathbb{A}_k \times \mathbb{A}_k \to \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z} \cong S^1.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi v
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = (x_v)_{v \in P}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi v
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y = (y_v)_{v \in P}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mi v
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle x, y \rangle \coloneqq \prod_v \langle x_v, y_v \rangle_v
          %p
            where each local pairing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -, - \rangle_v
            is defined to be a composite of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi v
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi v
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi mult
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi v
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi Tr
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Q
                    %mi v
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mi v
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_v \times k_v \stackrel{mult}{\to} k_v \stackrel{Tr}{\to} \mathbf{Q}_v \stackrel{\chi_v}{\to} \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z} \cong S^1,
          %p
            noting that a place
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            restricts to a place on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
          .num_remarks
            %h6#remarks Remarks
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The trace map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Tr
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tr
                  on the finite algebraic extension
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Q
                          %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_v/\mathbf{Q}_v
                  is of course defined by
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Tr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi σ
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tr(x) = \sum_\sigma \sigma(x)
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  ranges over all embeddings of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_v
                  into the algebraic closure of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℚ
                            %mi v
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}_v
              %li
                %p
                  When
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                  is the archimedean place on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℚ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi χ
                          %mi v
                        %mo :
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo →
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_v: \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}
                  to be not the quotient map, but its
                  = succeed "." do
                    %em additive inverse
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                          %mo =
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v = p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi χ
                          %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_p
                  is the composite
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Q
                          %mi p
                        %mo →
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi p
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Q}_p \to \mathbb{Z}(p^\infty) \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}
                  as defined
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/p-adic+number#duality"} here
              %li
                %p
                  For each
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔸
                            %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in \mathbb{A}_k
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi v
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi y
                          %mi v
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mi v
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle x_v, y_v \rangle_v = 1 \in S^1
                  for all but finitely many places
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi v
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi y
                          %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_v, y_v \in \mathcal{O}_v
                  for all but finitely many places. Hence
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle x, y\rangle
                  is well-defined.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              The additive group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+duality"} Pontrjagin self-dual
              in the sense that the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi: \mathbb{A}_k \to \mathbb{A}_k^\wedge
              induced from the pairing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle-, -\rangle
              is an isomorphism onto the character group.
          %p
            Moreover, define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∧
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi: \mathbb{A}_k \to k^\wedge
            to be the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi k
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi ϕ
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∧
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∧
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k \stackrel{\phi}{\to} \mathbb{A}_k^\wedge \stackrel{i^\wedge}{\to} k^\wedge.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              The map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \circ i: k \to k^\wedge
              vanishes. The map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k/k \to k^\wedge
              induced by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi: \mathbb{A}_k \to k^\wedge
              is an isomorphism of topological groups, so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k/k
              is Pontrjagin dual to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %h3#FunctionFieldAnalogy Function field analogy
          %p
            Via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy"} function field analogy
            one may understand any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+field"} number field
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field"} function field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            as being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+functions"} rational functions
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+curve"} arithmetic curve
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_F
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            has the interpretation of being the ring of functions on all punctured
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+disks"} formal disks
            around all points of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Frenkel05"} Frenkel 05, section 3.2
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AsRestrictedProduct"}
            above.
          %p
            This means for instance that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_n(\mathbb{A}_F)
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in the ring of adeles has the interpretation as being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cocycles
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+vector+bundles"} algebraic vector bundles
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+curve"} algebraic curve
            with respect to any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            of that curve by the complement of a finite number of points together with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+disks"} formal disks
            around these points. (Notice that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
